<title>RUSSIA: WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - Jan 24.</title>
<headline>WEATHER - Conditions at CIS airports - Jan 24.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Airports in central and northern Russia, western Siberia and the Volga River region could be closed on January 24 and 25 due to strong winds, low clouds and heavy snow, the Russian Weather Service said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The probability of the airports closing down was between 60 and 70 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Flights could be postponed at airports on the Kamchatka peninsula and Magadan in Russia's Far East on January 24 because of high winds and snowstorms, the service said.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
